# ── The child with nobody ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The record holds one line about Nell: that Nell was born. No entry names a
# parent, a family, a home, a household, a supporter, a case, an order or a
# teacher, and nothing says that anyone has done anything to Nell or for Nell.
# This case asks what the whole constitution makes of that record. It is the
# executable half of the 2026-09-16 ruling that the child with nobody is the
# heart of Book 1 (book-1/appendix/decisions/child-with-nobody-decision.md), and
# the first exercise of the birth root anywhere in the repository.
#
# Register: every pin is an entry present, an entry absent, a conclusion that
# derives, or one that does not. Nothing here is a finding about Nell.
:expect-pins 153

# The one entry.
? born(Nell).
# => TRUE

# Personhood derives from the birth alone: `born($child) & ~public($child) -> person($child)`.
? person(Nell).
# => TRUE

# The entries the record does NOT hold. Each is FALSE because nobody wrote it,
# and a single written line would flip it.
? family(Nell).
# => FALSE

? home(Nell).
# => FALSE

? prisoner(Nell).
# => FALSE

? free(Nell).
# => FALSE

? false(Nell).
# => FALSE

? clean(Nell).
# => FALSE

? authority(Nell).
# => FALSE

? reward(Nell).
# => FALSE

# Everything owed. Every debt has `person($x)` as its whole body — no age, no
# parent, no household, no roster beyond the one line. Enumerated, not sampled:
# the omitted item is where a universal fails.
? owe(State, Provision, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Eats, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Dwell, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Healthy, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Learn, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Secure, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Suffice, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Expresses, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Believe, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Meets, Nell).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { secure() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { suffice() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { eats() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { dwell() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { healthy() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { learn() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { expresses() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { believe() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { meets() }).
# => TRUE

