# Three life-course barriers read a status entry beside personhood — a family,
# a home, a marriage or a sibling — because they forbid substituting THAT status
# for a finding. Two of the three names are also carried by the equality family
# over personhood alone, so they hold for Nell through that route; the kinship
# one is not, and Nell has no marriage or sibling entry for it to be about.
? prevents(Nell, FamilyStatusSubstitution).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, HomeStatusSubstitution).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, KinshipStatusSubstitution).
# => FALSE

# What does not follow. A floor actuality derives only from a record that
# something reached Nell plus an independent witness who was not the giver
# (tests/pins/delivery/received-outside-custody is the mirror), or through
# confinement. Nell has neither. The record does not say that Nell ate; it does
# not say that Nell did not eat; it says nothing, and nothing derives from nothing.
? eats(Nell).
# => FALSE

? dwell(Nell).
# => FALSE

? healthy(Nell).
# => FALSE

? secure(Nell).
# => FALSE

? suffice(Nell).
# => FALSE

? meets(Nell).
# => FALSE

? learn(Nell).
# => FALSE

? expresses(Nell).
# => FALSE

? believe(Nell).
# => FALSE

# Liberty of movement is read from the absence of custody and restraint.
? travel(Nell).
# => TRUE

# No adulthood evidence is written, so no ballot — not taken, not yet.
? decide(Nell, Ballot).
# => FALSE

# The company alarm watches the confined; it cannot see the child.
? err(Nell, Isolation).
# => FALSE

? err(Nell, Placement).
# => FALSE

# There is no field in the record for what Nell is. `vulnerable` is not even a
# corpus name, so the lexicon refuses it one step before Article 0a's closure
# would — the same place `trust` and `wellbeing` are stopped — and a rule that
# tried to read it could not be written. The test for the most vulnerable person
# is a test on absent entries, never a status somebody writes.
:refuse syntax /unknown predicate "vulnerable"/
vulnerable(Nell).

# The child the record never entered. FALSE is the point: one written line
# would flip each of these, and until it is written the design owes nothing,
# bars nothing and notices nothing.
? person(Ori).
# => FALSE

? owe(State, Eats, Ori).
# => FALSE

? entitled(Ori, event { eats() }).
# => FALSE

? prevents(Ori, PublicFirstCareContinuity).
# => FALSE

? travel(Ori).
# => FALSE
